# Repo-level shellcheck policy.
#
# CI runs:
#   shellcheck -x -S warning $(find . -name '*.sh' \
#       -not -path './vm-setup/third-party/*' \
#       -not -path './lab/*')
#
# The `-x` flag follows `source`/`.` directives, so the lib/ helpers
# get checked in the context of the script that includes them.
#
# Note: no repo-wide rule suppressions are configured here. Both
# previously-suppressed checks (SC1091 for dynamic source paths, SC2148
# for source-only fragments) are handled with narrowly-scoped
# annotations at the actual call sites:
#
#   - SC1091:  `# shellcheck source=path/to/file` on the few `source`
#              lines whose target is dynamic (e.g. backend dispatch in
#              setup.sh).
#   - SC2148:  `# shellcheck shell=bash` directives at the top of the
#              source-only fragments under vm-setup/lib/.
#
# Keeping the config narrow means CI will still catch newly-introduced
# bad source paths or new .sh files that ship without a shebang or
# shell directive.
